From 5abd5a985ed9e2a1a6a02c3052fcc118993e649a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Grasso <me@leonardograsso.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:10:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(mermaid-text): cross subgraph borders, never follow them

Subgraph borders were ordinary cells for edge routing, so an edge leaving a subgraph could travel along its border row or column, past its corners and through its title, which reads as part of the border. Border line cells now admit only a perpendicular move and must be left straight through; corners and title cells are closed. The Manhattan fallback still applies when no such route exists.
