index 1934873..14fa508 100644
--- a/crates/mermaid-text/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/crates/mermaid-text/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -20,6 +20,9 @@ This project adheres to [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/)
 
 ### Changed
 
+- Edges cross a subgraph border perpendicularly at one cell and no longer
+  travel along a border, past its corners or through its title. When no
+  such route exists, the existing Manhattan fallback still applies.
 - Sequence lifelines are solid (`│`) and joined to messages: the source end
   of a message is a junction (`├`/`┤`), a lifeline it crosses becomes `┼`,
   and the arrowhead sits next to the target's lifeline, which stays drawn.
